  "body": "**Stacked on #2112** (rest Adaptive, `mkinney:issue/2031-rest-adaptive`, head 71a7fee47). This PR's own change is its last commit (ee0405765). Until #2112 merges, the diff against main also shows #2112's commits. Merge #2112 first. Not stacked on #2114 (#2113's pins); the two touch different hunks of `tests/rest_adaptive/sim.rs`.\n\n## What changed\n\nAll in `crates/motion/src/machining2d/adaptive/`:\n\n1. **Retrace lead** (`rest/leads.rs`).\n   - A rest pass can now be reached by going back along the pass just cut: the same chords reversed, which the exact-sign crossing law reads as a collinear retrace and never a crossing. It stops at the new run's start where the last pass went over it; otherwise it goes to that pass's wall landing and on along the wall.\n   - Every lead is offered stay-down first, least air first; retract leads keep their old order.\n   - The old wall stretch is still offered. Every lead is still asked the centre-area law, the crossing law and the load walk.\n   - The retrace is a feed at the cut depth and never a plunge, so the entry guard is untouched.\n2. **Cells** (`rest/peel.rs`, `TILE_PER_D = 4`). An area is planned in cells at most 4 tool diameters wide. The neck's one area, which held both mouths and the neck, used to cut one mouth and then the other in every phase, with a retract between.\n3. **Travel budget, refused by name** (`rest/budget.rs`, new).\n   - Feed out of cut is at most 3.0x the feed in cut, per depth.\n   - Retract hops are at most one per rest area after the first, plus the plain Adaptive's `HOP_BUDGET` (8).\n   - The yardstick is what the passes remove: a chord is in cut where it clears, on average, at least a graze (0.5% of D) of the rest material planned to be cut. It uses `Raster::cut_count`, new in `raster/conservative.rs`.\n   - I did not use the plain Adaptive's `lift::travel` yardstick: it reads wall rides as cut. The old plan scored 402 mm in cut against 194 mm out of cut on it, so a budget on that reading would bind nothing.\n   - The figures go into each depth's note.\n4. `docs/decisions/2109-rest-adaptive-air.md`: the decision, readings, and what was dropped (lifted returns, chord shortcuts, trimming the run margins, arc fit).\n\n#2108 is not needed: this changes how passes are reached, not what sharp corners or necks get.\n\n## Readings\n\nDebug build, 4 mm tool after a 12 mm tool, two depths. Cut / air feed / rapid are in mm, from the test's independent column stock.\n\n| Fixture | Before | After | Plunges a depth | Planner out/in (one depth) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 60 x 40, 3 mm corners | 224 / 967 / 360 | 328 / 562 / 359 | 4 -> 4 | 4.1x -> 2.8x |\n| 70 x 50, island, 2 pillars | 250 / 955 / 450 | 388 / 485 / 452 | 4 -> 4 | 4.0x -> 2.6x |\n| two bays, 10 mm neck | 954 / 3445 / 1337 | 1438 / 1979 / 545 | 37 -> 10 | 3.6x -> 2.7x |\n\n- **Cut length.** The test's cut figure rises because a retrace rides the wall the last pass left, and that contact reads as cut. On the planner's removal yardstick, in-cut is unchanged (117 / 121 / 467 mm a depth).\n- **Moves.** 3216 -> 4064 (corner) and 14850 -> 17840 (neck). The output is still chords; arc fit is not in this PR.\n- **Load.** The neck's worst measured load is 15.38% of D, against the planner's own bound of 15.377% (optimal x 1.05, unchanged). Before it read 15.05%. Measured and planner grids are aligned (D/120), so this reading sits right at the planner's limit by design. It is the closest any fixture comes to its `LOAD_SLACK`; please look at this one.\n\n## How tested\n\nPins:\n\n- `four_corner_residues_...`: air feed at most 2x the cut.\n- `an_island_...`: air feed at most 1.5x the cut.\n- `a_neck_the_earlier_tool_...`: at most 24 plunges, air feed at most 1.6x the cut.\n- `machining2d::adaptive::rest::tests::the_travel_budget_refuses_by_name_past_each_limit` (unit).\n\nMutations:\n\n- Without the retrace, the corner and neck plans are refused by the budget, and the island fails its air assertion.\n- Without the cells, the neck is refused (22 hops against 16).\n\nGates:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: motion and app suites ok (10.4 min).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean on the final head. Clippy's doc-list lint and an unused test field were fixed after the gate run; `rest_adaptive` and `adaptive::rest` were re-run green on the final head.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Run on macOS only.\n- The budget was not tried on shapes beyond the fixtures. A real part that travels more is refused by name (\"rest Adaptive at Z.. would feed .. mm out of cut .. (over 3.0x) - choose Waterline or Offset rings\"). Rest Adaptive is not wired into the Pocket operation until #2033.\n\nChangelog: rest Adaptive reaches each pass back along the one before it and is held to a travel budget (out-of-cut feed at most 3x the cut, one retract per rest area plus 8), refused by name past it (#2109)\nEffort: high (not escalated)\n\nFixes #2109\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
